      "content": "That quiet, drifting feeling is your mind's way of telling you it's time to stop fighting for a moment. You're not a ghost—you're just a person who has been holding on for far too long, and it's okay to let that weight slip. If you can't feel your hands, maybe you don't need to use them for anything heavy right now. Just let yourself be still, and when you're ready, you can take a small step—even if it's just to feel the cold floor under your feet.",
